[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]

; The dining chair, from Models/tablechair/TableChair.fbx. Replaces pf_chair.
;
; SCALE 0.22 puts it at 0.48 x 0.91 x 0.44, against the 0.46 x 0.96 x 0.44 CSG
; chair it replaces -- near enough that every one of the fifteen placements
; still tucks under the table it was measured for.
;
; This one does NOT share the armchair's scale, and should not: the couch and
; the club chair are one set built from the same model stretched, where a
; mismatch in seat height reads instantly. A dining chair is a different piece
; of furniture and is sized against the table instead.
;
; The FBX ships a DirectionalLight3D called Sun inside it. Fifteen of those in
; one house would have flattened the lighting completely; TableChair.fbx.import
; skips that node. It also maps both the model's materials -- "Wood" and
; "Material.001" -- onto the single atlas they share.
;
; Measured from the mesh VERTICES, not get_aabb(), which through a rotated
; transform returns the bound of the rotated box and is inflated.

